#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
btaudiod -- Bluetooth audio-out manager for the Xiegu X6200.

The stock X6200 GUI pairs Bluetooth devices over QtBluetooth but only for CAT
(serial/RFCOMM) work; it has no concept of routing the radio's audio to an A2DP
headset.  This daemon provides exactly that, plus a small JSON API the QML
front-end drives.

How the audio gets there
------------------------
The X6200's demodulated audio arrives from the FPGA on the SoC codec's capture
side, which is exposed as the ALSA PCM ``mixcapture`` (a dsnoop, so several
readers may share it).  The stock UI plays it straight to ALSA, bypassing
PulseAudio -- which is why nothing shows up in PA while the radio talks.

We therefore never touch the radio's own playback path.  Instead we *tap*
``mixcapture`` and loop it into the Bluetooth sink that PulseAudio creates when
an A2DP headset connects::

    mixcapture  ->  module-loopback  ->  bluez_sink.<MAC>.a2dp_sink  ->  headset

Both ends are PulseAudio modules, so rate conversion and latency are handled for
us and the radio keeps playing to its speaker (and over Bluetooth) untouched.

BlueZ is driven directly over D-Bus (synchronously -- no GLib main loop is
available on this Buildroot image).  Pairing is delegated to ``bluetoothctl``
because that gives us a working pairing agent for free.

Run as root.  Control surface:  http://127.0.0.1:8637/state  ,  POST /cmd
"""

